Package: startup-time-checker
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: hold boot until a chosen time (self-imposed lockout)
 A small systemd service that runs early in boot and refuses to let the
 machine finish starting until a time set with "startup-time set" has passed,
 for example "tomorrow 07:00".
 .
 The startup-time command is setuid root so an ordinary user can set a lock.
 Non-root users can only extend an active lock, never shorten or clear it.
